{
  "_readme": "Approved Sinhala vocabulary for GearGrid. Translate FROM this list so the same English term always gets the same Sinhala word. The auto-translate script (npm run i18n:translate) feeds this file to the model. To change a term app-wide: edit it here, then re-run translation for the affected keys.",
  "audience": "Equipment-rental shop staff, cashiers, managers and accountants in Sri Lanka, many of whom read Sinhala more comfortably than English.",
  "style": [
    "Natural, polite, plain written Sinhala as used in everyday business software. Not heavily literary or Sanskritised, and never a word-for-word calque of the English.",
    "Buttons and actions: imperative ending in -න්න (e.g. සුරකින්න, මකන්න). Field labels and headings: nouns.",
    "Success messages: past formal passive (…කරන ලදී.). Failure messages: …අසාර්ථක විය. Missing/invalid input: …අවශ්‍යයි / …වලංගු නොවේ.",
    "Confirmations are questions: …ඔබට විශ්වාසද?",
    "Keep brand and technical tokens in Latin script: GearGrid, LKR, Rs., CSV, XLSX, PDF, QR, POS, SKU, URL, API, ID.",
    "Always preserve {{placeholders}}, markup tags such as <b>, <strong>, <hl>, and leave the English text of language names alone.",
    "Counts take the -ක් counter where natural ({{count}}ක්). _one and _other plural forms are usually identical in Sinhala.",
    "Numbers stay in Western digits. Do not translate currency symbols.",
    "Short UI labels must stay short: prefer one or two words over a descriptive phrase."
  ],
  "keepEnglish": [
    "GearGrid",
    "LKR",
    "Rs.",
    "CSV",
    "XLSX",
    "PDF",
    "QR",
    "POS",
    "SKU",
    "URL",
    "API",
    "ID",
    "SMS",
    "CORS",
    "IP",
    "DB"
  ],
